## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to enforce data quality at ingestion in a beginner OTCA setting, with per-tenant controls and end-to-end lifecycle.

## Key Concepts

- Ingest-time validation and whitelist
- Idempotency and dedup
- Per-tenant partitioning in storage
- Auditability of dropped records

## Code Example

```javascript
function validate(event, knownTenants){
  if(!event.tenant_id || !knownTenants.includes(event.tenant_id)) return false;
  if(!['login','click','error','latency'].includes(event.event_type)) return false;
  const ts = new Date(event.timestamp);
  const now = new Date();
  if(isNaN(ts) || Math.abs(now - ts) > 7*24*60*60*1000) return false;
  if(event.latency_ms != null && event.latency_ms < 0) return false;
  return true;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema evolution at ingestion without breaking existing pipelines?
- How would you implement a lightweight audit log for dropped events and partial successes?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design privacy-first OTCA paths that enforce data residency, tenant isolation, and masking, going beyond basic streaming.

## Key Concepts

- OTCA data contracts, regional immutable storage, global masked aggregates
- Per-tenant masking (tokenization, redaction) and tenant-key management
- Data lineage, access controls, and residency verification

## Code Example

```javascript
function maskRecord(record, tenantKey) {
  const masked = { ...record };
  if (masked.email) masked.email = hash(masked.email + tenantKey);
  if (masked.phone) masked.phone = redact(masked.phone);
  // redact other PII fields as needed
  return masked;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test masking correctness and residency under synthetic bursts?
- How do you handle schema evolution for masked fields across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Gauges understanding of privacy-at-ingest, per-tenant residency, and practical, testable workflows for OTCA telemetry in mobile apps.

## Key Concepts
- Ingest-time policy evaluation
- Per-tenant residency and data partitioning
- Edge gateway to regional streaming
- Deterministic event ordering and testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPayload(category, payload, policy){
  const out = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(payload));
  const cfg = policy[category] || {};
  if (cfg.redact) {
    for (const field of cfg.redact){ delete out[field]; }
  }
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify per-tenant data residency after changes?
- How would you evolve the schema for new diagnostics fields?
